        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google): anchor model-ID regexes to prevent false-positive substring matches",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n**Problem**: Model-ID matching in `google-shared.ts` uses unanchored substring patterns:\n- `model.id.includes(\"2.5-pro\")` matches `gemini-2.5-pro-exp` and `not-gemini-2.5-pro`\n- `/gemini-3(?:\\.\\d+)?-pro/` matches `not-gemini-3-pro-vision`\n- `/gemma-?4/` matches `not-gemma-4-pro`\n\nThese false-positives can silently route the wrong thinking budget/config to a different model variant.\n\n**Solution**: Anchor all model-ID regexes with `(?:^|\\/)` prefix and `\\b` word boundary suffix. Also replace `String.includes()` calls with properly anchored regex tests.\n\n**Per ClawSweeper review**: The MIME type validation (previously in this PR) has been **removed**. Only the regex anchoring fixes remain.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n```\n$ npx tsx _validate-regex-anchors.mts\n=== Model-ID regex anchoring proof ===\n\n  ✓ gemma-4: \"models/gemma-4\" → true (valid match)\n  ✓ gemma-4 substring: \"not-gemma-4-pro\" → false (OLD false positive, NEW rejected)\n  ✓ gemini-3-pro: \"models/gemini-3-pro\" → true (valid match)\n  ✓ gemini-3-pro substring: \"not-gemini-3-pro-vision\" → false (OLD false positive, NEW rejected)\n  ✓ gemini-3-flash: \"models/gemini-3-flash\" → true (valid match)\n  ✓ gemini-3-flash substring: \"not-gemini-3-flash-lite\" → false (OLD false positive, NEW rejected)\n  ✓ gemini-2.5-pro valid: \"models/gemini-2.5-pro\" → true\n  ✓ gemini-2.5-pro substring: \"not-gemini-2.5-pro-exp\" → false\n  ✓ gemini-2.5-flash-lite: \"models/gemini-2.5-flash-lite\" → true\n  ✓ gemini-2.5-flash-lite substring: \"not-gemini-2.5-flash-lite-x\" → false\n  ✓ gemini-2.5-flash: \"models/gemini-2.5-flash\" → true\n  ✓ gemini-2.5-flash vs flash-lite: \"models/gemini-2.5-flash-lite\" → false (NOT matched as flash)\n\n✅ 12 passed, 0 failed\n```\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- `pnpm build:ci-artifacts` → exit 0 ✓\n- Existing google-shared test suite passes (including updated regex tests)\n\n/cc @openclaw/clawsweeper",
        "branch": "fix/google-regex-anchors",
